      "message": "Verdict: hardware-verification note, effectively already tracked; no code change needed.\n\nYour code reading is right - send_one_time_boot (badfish.py:1123) and patch_boot_seq (badfish.py:810, seq cached by get_boot_devices) both key off the current committed BootMode (get_bios_boot_mode, badfish.py:228-247), so on a same-reset mode switch both legs carry old-mode keys. But the failure is conditional on one unverifiable firmware behavior (does iDRAC honor old-mode one-time/seq keys on the same-reset switch?), which is exactly #737 item 3, and item 3 already names both of your options: (a) two-phase, (b) derive from desired mode.\n\nThe new delta is the persistent BootSources leg. It is written and applied by change_boot (badfish.py:769-779) with its own config job and reboot while the host is still in the old mode, so it is correct at apply time; it only becomes stale because of the later mode switch. Same root cause, same conditional, and second-order: if the one-time leg fails, the rebuild is broken regardless of the persistent order.\n\nNeither remedy fits KISS: (a) two-phase does not fix the persistent leg (BootSources order is still configured pre-switch in prepare_host_hardware; moving it post-switch is a move-flow redesign) and leaves a mid-flow reboot with no PXE override; (b) is not expressible with the current data - idrac_interfaces.yml has one device-name list per model and names are mode-specific (NIC.PxeDevice.* vs NIC.Integrated.*), and check_device (badfish.py:1183-1191) validates against the current-mode sequence (why the deeper review rejected the merged-PATCH variant).\n\nIf the verification run shows the one-time leg failing, the mode-agnostic option already in tree is set_next_boot_pxe (System.BootSourceOverrideTarget: Pxe/Once; interfaces/hardware.py:87, dispatchers/hardware.py:229): one PATCH, no BootMode dependence, no yaml change.\n\nFolded the persistent leg into #737 so the single verification run covers it. Keeping the change as-is: minimal, fail-safe (aborts on read/set failure), and never-kickstarted hosts are already flagged post-rebuild (c9f60c34).",
